body:
Just my two cents, but probably a good idea to make a method for this in case it needs to be checked for more kinds of input events in the future, or more changes to it need to be done. Also helps reducing the complexity of the long line and results in cleaner code imo.
```cpp
bool _is_pressing_inside(position) {
  return has_point(position) && get_viewport_transform().xform(get_viewport_rect()).has_point(position);
  // Maybe even split this in two separate bool checks to reduce line length
  // but this is more unnecessary imo:
  // const bool is_in_viewport = get_viewport...
  // return has_point(position) && is_in_viewport;
}
```
and then just
```cpp
status.pressing_inside = _is_pressing_insde(touch->get_position()); // or drag->get_position
```
